The function is already a single compare-and-set; I kept the comparison but express it as an unsigned range check against `FIT_UINT16_INVALID`, which is equivalent for all `uint16` values and lets the compiler emit a branchless `setb` without a 16-bit immediate compare against `0xFFFF`.

```cpp
FIT_BOOL Field::IsValid(void) const
{
    return static_cast<FIT_BOOL>(profileIndex < FIT_UINT16_INVALID);
}
```